# Building and testing

Build the command from the workspace root:

```sh
./compile.sh
```

This creates `./executable`. The implementation is written in Go and uses only
its standard library, so the build is offline and has no third-party package
dependencies. The Go module is kept in `src/` so it does not change how Go
commands interpret the workspace root.

Run the regression tests with:

```sh
(cd src && go test ./...)
```

The implementation includes a streaming line editor, ANSI styling, preference
file loading and YAML parsing. Ordinary Go commands are passed to the Go
compiler/toolchain; test output is processed independently on stdout and stderr.
Generated executables and development artifacts are excluded by `.gitignore`.
EOF
